# AGENTS.md

Subagent definitions for the agentic-workflow plugin. Invoke these from the harness
(subagent picker or Task tool) to keep the main thread focused.

Definitions are symlinked by `bootstrap/install.sh`:
- **Claude Code:** `.claude/agents/` — loaded natively as project subagents.
- **Cursor:** `.cursor/agents/` — reference symlinks (source:
  `~/.cursor/plugins/local/agentic-workflow/agents/`, or the clone's `cursor/agents/`
  when the local plugin is not installed yet).

| Agent | Use when |
|---|---|
| **planner** | A risk-first implementation roadmap is needed in isolation (e.g. during `/plan-feature`) |
| **researcher** | Library or API research would bloat the main thread |
| **reviewer** | A findings-only code review is needed before fixing (e.g. during `/review-loop`) |
| **pr-reviewer** | A scored PR review (0–5, eight dimensions) before posting a PR comment |
| **enterprise-reviewer** | A deep principles audit (DDD, modularity, dependency hygiene, OO, security) during `/enterprise-review` |
| **frontend-planner** | A risk-first frontend roadmap (Vue/Vite, DDD modules) during `/frontend:plan-feature` |
| **frontend-reviewer** | A findings-only frontend review (reactivity, a11y, library-first) during `/frontend:review-loop` |
| **pattern-analyst** | Extracting existing CRUD/component/store patterns during `/frontend:analyze-patterns` |

